  "built-in-power-and-fans": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "The product page lists two AC inputs, two PSU slots and two fans; the brochure says two 100 - 240 V power supplies with failover and temperature based fan control; the quick guide says power comes from two IEC connectors. No document held shows a removable supply module or gives a supply part number, and the rear photograph shows two bare inlets, so the supplies are built into the chassis and there are no bays, as on juniper/ex2300-24t. The two fans are the two hexagon grilles of the rear photograph. The photograph also shows a spring wire retaining clip on each inlet, which is a cord accessory and is not drawn."
  },
  "buttons": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "Two round buttons printed RESET and MODE (quick guide: the reset button, and a mode button that runs a RouterOS script). The drawing gives their centres. Both are drawn with the library's recessed reset-button part; the MODE one carries function mode."
  },
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "443 wide, 44 high, 193 deep: the drawing dimensions 443, 193 and 44. The brochure and the product page print 443 x 194 x 44 mm; the drawing's 193 is carried and the 194 is declared a conflict. The 6 mm the plan dimensions is the two cable loops standing off the rear, an accessory and not part of the depth. 443 is the body between the ear folds."
  },
  "colour": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "median of photograph 1526's face (#d9d9d9)."
  },
  "console": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "The RJ45 serial port (brochure: serial port RJ45; quick guide: 115200 bit/s) is the jack under the printed CONSOLE."
  },
